  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Calenduloside C may interact with CCRF-HSB-2 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Calenduloside C is predicted to act as a target for VMRC-LCP, which in turn is targeted by Tamarixinin B. This pathway leads to the final target CCRF-HSB-2. Similarly, Calenduloside C is also predicted to interact with SF-188, which is targeted by Exo-1,7,7-trimethylbicyclo[2.2.1]hept-2-yl acetate, which also ultimately targets CCRF-HSB-2. These findings indicate that Calenduloside C may exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways, both of which converge on CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Calenduloside C influences CCRF-HSB-2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Calenduloside C in the regulation of CCRF-HSB-2."
